title: Labels that show up close
intro: A Text can sit on a box fitted to its words, and a Show When can hide it when the camera pulls out.

project: Empty | World Labels

chapter: A box behind the words | Text > Background
create: Text
rename: Label
set: Transform.Position = 0, -1, 0
set: Text.Value = IDLE
set: Text.Size = 0.5
say: A label over a busy floor is hard to read. A Text can draw a box right behind its letters.
set: Text.Background = #CC101018
set: Text.Padding = 0.15
expectvalue: Label.Text.Padding = 0.15
explain: field:Text.Background | Background | Background is the color of a box fitted to the text's lines. Transparent, the default, draws none.
explain: field:Text.Padding | Padding | Padding is how far the box reaches past the letters on every side, in world units.
set: Text.Value = UNLOADING C05-1 3/4
explain: scene | Scene view | The box grows with the words, and shrinks again with a shorter label.
set: Text.Value = FEEDING C03\n2/4
say: It is fitted to every line, and follows Align and Vertical Align too.

chapter: Only when zoomed in | Show When > Zoom Below
create: Sprite
rename: Worker
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0.5, 0
select: Label
add: ShowWhen
set: ShowWhen.ZoomBelow = 7
expectvalue: Label.ShowWhen.ZoomBelow = 7
explain: field:ShowWhen.ZoomBelow | Zoom Below | With Zoom Below at seven, the label shows while the camera's Size is seven or less, and is hidden when the camera pulls out. Zero ignores the zoom.
say: The worker's sprite has no Show When, so it stays at every zoom. No flag is needed for a zoom alone.
select: Main Camera
set: Camera.Size = 9
play
wait: 1
say: The camera is at nine, so the label is gone and the worker shows.
stop
set: Camera.Size = 6
play
wait: 1
say: Zoomed in to six, the label is back on its box.
stop
